.TH SHBAR 1 "2026-11-18" "shbar 1.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
shbar \- a divider and status or header bar for the terminal

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shbar
.RB [ \-bhilmnruv ]
.RB [ \-c\ char ]
.RB [ \-p\ text ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shbar
is a small C program that can be used as a visual divider, header,
or bottom status bar in a terminal.

The generated bar always extends to the current terminal width.

Several options are available for customizing the appearance and
alignment of the bar text.

.B shbar
is part of the
.B shui-tools
collection.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-b
Display bar text in bold.

.TP
.BI "\-c " char
Use a different filler character.
The default filler is a space character.

.TP
.B \-h
Show a short usage message.

.TP
.B \-i
Display bar text in italic.

.TP
.B \-l
Left align the text.

.TP
.B \-m
Pad only half of the terminal width.

.TP
.B \-n
Return
.IR columns \- length_of_text .

.TP
.BI "\-p " text
Text displayed within the bar.

.TP
.B \-r
Right align the text.

.TP
.B \-u
Display bar text underlined.

.TP
.B \-v
Display bar text in reverse video.

.SH EXAMPLES
Display a status bar:

.PP
.nf
status="[ load 3% : t/sec 49 : source.c ] "
shbar -p "${status}"
.fi

.PP
Display a bold heading before showing output:

.PP
.nf
shbar -bp "Result as follows: " -c " "
cat result.txt | less -r +G
.fi

